== Question 3: the mean and the standard deviation of the scaler
sd of the vibration: all 315 readings 0.959, the 300 clean ones 0.831; sd of the temperature 10.772 against 10.543
median and MAD-based scale of the vibration, all 315: 1.484, 0.973
a batch of 50 idle readings with the temperature drifted by +8 deg C (2.7 sd of the idle mode):
  scaled with the training mean and sd      : flagged 9 of 50
  scaled with its own mean and sd (the leak): flagged 30 of 50;  the mean of the scaled temperatures -0.0
  scaled with the training scaler, mean z of the temperature: -0.23
  scaler fitted on training + batch: flagged 5 of 50 with the old detector
  scaler fitted on training + batch and the detector refitted in that space: flagged 10 of 50
a batch of 50 faulty readings:
  scaled with the training mean and sd      : flagged 50 of 50
  scaled with its own mean and sd (the leak): flagged 28 of 50; mean of the scaled batch [-0. -0.]  sd [1. 1.]
  sd of the faulty batch [16.61  1.43] against the training sd [10.54  0.83]

== Question 4: ten million readings with 20 features
forest, 100 trees, psi = 256: fit on 20 000 rows 0.34 s;  scoring 200 000 rows 2.93 s -> 10^7 rows about 147 s (single process)
forest fit on 200 000 rows (psi still 256): 1.93 s
LOF (k = 20) fit on 20 000 rows: 4.63 s; the neighbour search is quadratic, so 10^7 rows would take about 1.2e+06 s = 13 days
LOF (k = 20) fitted on 20 000 rows: scoring 5 000 rows 1.23 s -> 10^7 rows about 2452 s = 0.7 h
Nystroem(100) + SGDOneClassSVM, 5 epochs on 200 000 rows: fit 9.74 s, scoring 200 000 rows 6.58 s -> 10^7 rows: fit about 487 s, scoring about 329 s
book timing of the exact one-class SVM: slope of ln t against ln n over the last three sizes: 2.12
   extrapolated to 10^7 rows from 5.794 s at 40 000: 7.1e+05 s = 8 days
book timing of Nystroem + SGD: slope over the last three sizes: 1.72  (30 epochs, 100 landmarks)
